<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="fit-title">Questions that decide it</h2>
      <dl class="fit-list">
        <div><dt>Who will do the entries?</dt><dd>Many accountants already know Tally. Ask the person you plan to hire what they actually use.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Do you carry much stock?</dt><dd>Test your real stock and billing steps in a trial. Do not rely on a feature list.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Do you want to see figures from anywhere?</dt><dd>A browser product does this by default. An installed product may need an add-on.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>What does it cost over three years?</dt><dd>Compare totals, including users, renewals and any accountant's charges.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Safe access for your accountant</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Buy the licence or subscription in your own name</li>
        <li>Give each person their own login, not a shared one</li>
        <li>Limit each role to what they need</li>
        <li>Know where the data file or account lives</li>
        <li>Take backups you can open yourself</li>
        <li>Remove access the day someone leaves</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="para">Tally's and Zoho's own help pages explain their user controls. Ask to be shown yours.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="move-title">
  <div class="wrap layout-side">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="move-title" class="first-h2">If you are moving from one to the other</h2>
      <p>Moving data is a project, and a cut-off date is what makes it manageable. Zoho publishes a {% ext "https://www.zoho.com/in/books/help/migration/tally-to-zoho-books.html", "Tally to Zoho Books guide" %}, based on exporting masters, vouchers and a trial balance from Tally and importing them.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Pick a clean cut-off, ideally a year or quarter end.</li>
        <li>Reconcile the bank, parties and stock in the old system first. Do not migrate errors.</li>
        <li>Move opening balances, and decide whether old transactions need to move at all.</li>
        <li>Check the trial balance on both sides after the move.</li>
        <li>Keep the old data, in a readable form, for as long as the record-keeping rules require.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="work">What accounting help in software usually covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Setting up the company, ledgers, tax settings and stock items</li>
        <li>Entering vouchers and reconciling bank statements</li>
        <li>Reports such as trial balance, profit and loss and party balances</li>
        <li>Correcting past errors, which is often a one-off project</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Knowing the software is not the same as understanding accounts or tax. Ask about both. Software features also do not replace the filing duties discussed under {% routeLink "/services/gst-return-filing/", "GST return filing" %}.</p>

      <h2 id="flags">Warning signs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Offers a cracked or unlicensed copy to save money</li>
        <li>Keeps your company file on their own laptop, with no copy for you</li>
        <li>Shares one login across staff</li>
        <li>Deletes or overwrites old entries without notes, particularly near filing time</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="fees">What affects the fee</h2>
      <p>Voucher volume, stock detail, migration or clean-up, and training. Software cost is separate from any accountant's fee, so ask for both in writing.</p>
